<%- include("partials/layout-start", { title: "Help" }) %>

<section class="page-head">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">new here?</p>
    <h1>How modify.at works.</h1>
    <p class="hero-text">
      A mod is a fan-made change for a game. It can add new content, change how something looks, fix a problem, or give players a new way to play.
    </p>
  </div>
  <a class="primary-link" href="/mods">Browse mods</a>
</section>

<section class="help-grid">
  <article class="help-card">
    <h2>Finding Mods</h2>
    <p>Use the Mods page to search by name, game, creator, or category. Open a mod page to read what it does before downloading it.</p>
  </article>

  <article class="help-card">
    <h2>Safe vs Unverified</h2>
    <p><strong>Safe</strong> means an admin reviewed the mod listing. <strong>Unverified</strong> means it is public, but has not been checked yet.</p>
  </article>

  <article class="help-card">
    <h2>Downloading</h2>
    <p>Click Download on a mod page. Only download mods you trust, and follow the creator's install instructions if they included any.</p>
  </article>

  <article class="help-card">
    <h2>Accounts</h2>
    <p>You need an account to upload mods and comment. Browsing and downloading are open so guests can look around first.</p>
  </article>

  <article class="help-card">
    <h2>Uploading</h2>
    <p>Creators choose a game, category, version, description, and file. New uploads start as Unverified until an admin checks them.</p>
  </article>

  <article class="help-card">
    <h2>Comments</h2>
    <p>Comments are for questions, feedback, bug reports, and installation help. Keep them useful so creators can improve their mods.</p>
  </article>
</section>

<section class="help-strip">
  <div>
    <h2>Not sure where to start?</h2>
    <p>Browse the catalog first, open a mod that looks interesting, and check the Safe or Unverified label before downloading.</p>
  </div>
  <a class="secondary-link" href="/register">Create account</a>
</section>

<%- include("partials/layout-end") %>
